    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.79) anchors the LawDog lineup as our premier start, leveraging a prime #2 hole spot and a favorable matchup against Kay (xERA 4.51). He is joined by the high-upside trio of **Bryce Harper** (76.31), **Lawrence Butler** (70.63), and **Cal Raleigh** (68.80). **Lawrence Butler** is particularly compelling today; despite a park penalty, his +13% platoon edge against Martinez creates an elite ceiling. Meanwhile, **Dylan Beavers** (68.43) remains a must-start despite the minor speed-kill penalty from a strong opposing catcher, as his #1 lineup position and significant platoon advantage ensure he remains one of our primary conduits for runs and potential stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Yainer Diaz** (61.25). While his efficiency score sits comfortably in our \"Strong\" category, he was narrowly edged out of the active roster by the higher projected outputs of **Will Smith** and **Cal Raleigh**. Despite **Yainer Diaz** having a solid matchup against Lynch IV, the optimizer prioritized the specific stacking configurations of the infield and utility slots. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** closely, as his status remains \"Lineup Pending\"; should he be scratched, **Yainer Diaz** will immediately rotate into the starting lineup to ensure we do not lose at-bats. We are also maintaining standard caution with **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Dylan Beavers**, as their sprint-speed metrics are suppressed by the presence of an elite defensive catcher behind the plate, making their base-stealing opportunities slightly riskier today.",
